@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Network egress boundary — the three modes, and what makes a dangerous posture acceptable

node "Agent container" as CTR <<host>> {
  component "agent CLI\n(may run fully autonomous)" as AGENT <<app>>
}

node "Host-orchestrated sidecars" as SIDE <<host>> {
  component "proveo-egress\nTLS MITM · credential broker · flow log" as MITM <<app>>
  component "Squid\nenforcement proxy" as SQUID <<app>>
  component "Ollama sidecar\n--local-model" as OLLAMA <<app>>
  component "docker:dind\nsibling daemon (privileged)" as DIND <<error>>
}

cloud "Pinned model provider" as PROV <<cloud>>
cloud "Open web (docs, search)" as WEB <<cloud>>

AGENT ARROW_MAIN MITM : **firewall** (default)\nagent trusts the inspector CA
MITM ARROW_MAIN SQUID
AGENT ARROW_MAIN SQUID : **proxy** — no TLS inspection
AGENT ARROW_CLOUD WEB : **broker** — direct bridge\n(container boundary only)
SQUID ARROW_CLOUD PROV : write-allow: pinned provider only
SQUID ARROW_CLOUD WEB : read-allow: GET-shaped web
AGENT ARROW_OPTIONAL OLLAMA : NO_PROXY bypass\n(opencode · cecli)
AGENT ARROW_OPTIONAL DIND : ""dind:true"" + Dockerfiles in scope\n+ PROVEO_DIND=1

note right of MITM
  **Two purposes, both network-level:**
  # //No irreversible action without HITL// — write
    methods (pushes, publishes) denied except to the
    model provider; attempts are logged.
  # //No leaks to cloud providers// — inference egress is
    pinned to the allowlisted provider auto-detected from
    the key present, while web reads stay open so the
    agent can still gather context.

  This is what makes claudecode's
  ""--dangerously-skip-permissions"" an acceptable posture:
  the containment is the network, not the agent's manners.

  Method/path policy (read-allow / write-deny / DLP) on
  this same hop: _spec/internal/egresspolicy/*.puml
end note

note bottom of SQUID
  **One domain list, two enforcement points.** The operator's extra
  domains and the harness's own infrastructure endpoints merge into a
  single space-separated list that the egress layer feeds to //both// the
  Squid ACL and the policy's write allowlist. Two lists would drift, and
  a domain reachable by one hop but denied by the other is the hardest
  denial to read.

  What the list admits is a wider question than what the broker injects:
  the reachable set is the endpoints of //every// provider the allowlist
  admits, because a session may call any provider whose key is present.
  Reach and injection are separate axes — see
  ""_spec/internal/egress/egress-tiers\.puml"".
end note

note bottom of OLLAMA
  **Local-model exceptions.** cursor is vendor-pinned (no
  custom base URL). claudecode speaks the Anthropic API
  shape, not Ollama's OpenAI-compatible endpoint, so the
  sidecar is not a drop-in there.

  **An opt-in add-on, and //where// inference runs is a second
  decision.** The host models dir is resolved only when
  ""--local-model"" is requested; alongside it the run decides
  whether inference lands on the host's Ollama or in a sidecar,
  and whether that sidecar gets a GPU.

  **On macOS the sidecar loses the GPU, so inference moves to
  the host.** A Linux container cannot reach the Metal GPU, so
  an in-network sidecar runs CPU-only and is unusably slow,
  while the host's Ollama at ""host\.docker\.internal"" is
  GPU-accelerated. The redirection is honored **only in broker
  mode** (""egress\.buildBroker""); the locked tiers keep the
  isolated sidecar regardless. ""PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL_SIDECAR=1""
  forces the in-network sidecar even on macOS.

  **The sidecar is GPU-accelerated only on Linux with the NVIDIA
  container runtime registered in Docker**, which is what makes
  ""--gpus all"" a valid flag. Passing it without the runtime
  makes the sidecar fail to start, so the runtime list from
  ""docker info"" is probed and the flag added only on a positive
  match.
end note

note bottom of DIND
  Only for modes that can expose a daemon without
  defeating enforcement; otherwise proveo warns and
  skips. Lifecycle: ""internal/dind"".
end note

note top of AGENT
  Tier is selected per run (""proveo run --egress-mode open|allowlist|review""),
  credentials independently (""--credentials broker|forward"")
  for every harness with ""egress: true"" in its manifest.
  Each run writes a top-allowed / top-denied report.
end note
@enduml
